-- Fixture for "l4 batch: when a declared breach was observed".
--
-- Two declared breaches, both effective at 5 and both observed at 9, the
-- event that revealed the misses: R's, through Q's LEST, and a bare BREACH
-- BY Q beside it in a RAND. They tie on everything that chooses the anchor
-- but position, so the anchor is the first, whichever side it is written
-- on: R in the first trace, Q in the second. (unstable observes the bare
-- BREACH at 5, so there it is the anchor in both.)

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF P, Q, R
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF x, y

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bare right` MEANS PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 5 LEST ((PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 0 LEST BREACH BY R) RAND (BREACH BY Q))

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bare left` MEANS PARTY P MUST x WITHIN 5 LEST ((BREACH BY Q) RAND (PARTY Q MUST y WITHIN 0 LEST BREACH BY R))

#TRACE `bare right` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY R DOES x AT 9

#TRACE `bare left` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY R DOES x AT 9

@export default trivial entrypoint so batch has a function to call
alwaysTrue MEANS TRUE
